@startuml
!include _style.iuml
' Adapted from reviewed presentation sources: W2-delivery-ledgers, W3-07a; separate SQL commit / relay / consumer
skinparam dpi 110
skinparam defaultFontSize 18
skinparam ArrowFontSize 17
skinparam ClassAttributeFontSize 17
skinparam ClassStereotypeFontSize 15
skinparam NoteFontSize 16
skinparam LegendFontSize 15
skinparam titleFontSize 20
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam maxMessageSize 135
skinparam nodesep 18
skinparam ranksep 24
hide footbox
hide circle
title DP-2 · lost-send reply, replay and atomic acceptance
autonumber
database "Media DB\nMediaOutbox" as MD <<outbox>> $MEDIA
participant "sql\ndelivery" as D <<relay>> $INFRA
participant "SQS\nprocessing-commands" as Q <<queue>> $INFRA
participant "messaging\nprocessing" as P <<consumer>> $PROC
database "Processing DB\nProcessingInbox" as PD <<idempotent inbox>> $PROC
note over MD : direct_intake.finalize has committed\npin + Asset + MediaOutbox row.
... MediaRepair calls publish_commands → publish_due ...
loop each due outbox row, bounded by limit / deadline
 D -> MD : lock SKIP LOCKED; save claim token; COMMIT
 D -> Q : transport.send(queue, body)\n[SQS.send → send_message]
 alt send reply lost / network error
  D -> MD : fence matching claim token; retain row;\nretry the SAME message_id
 else acknowledged send
  D -> MD : fence matching token; sent_at;\nnext replay; COMMIT
 end
end
... event-source mapping delivers the record (first delivery or redelivery) ...
Q -> P : consume_batch → handle_command(factory, body)
group one Processing transaction
 P -> PD : accept: insert message_id + body_hash
 alt duplicate ID and identical body hash
  P --> Q : False; no domain mutation
 else conflicting body hash
  P -> PD : ROLLBACK; MessageConflict
  P --> Q : batch failure; redrive / DLQ
 else new command
  P -> PD : guard + Job + Attempt +\nwork/result outboxes; COMMIT
  P --> Q : True; record counts as success
 end
end
note over Q,PD
The relay never calls Processing directly. The event-source mapping
deletes only successful records. Processing's result outbox and
Media's inbox repeat the same local pattern.
end note
@enduml
